      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "MIKI MARK (1) was racing well without winning before making up plenty of ground to score at his latest appearance over 2180m at this track. Likely to get all the favours from this nice draw. Steps up a level but he is up to the task. WHERES WOOD WOOD (9) went back last start then worked home in good style to finish 6 metres from the winner in second at Shepparton over 1690m, that effort following a good win at Shepparton the run prior. Meets a comparable field and she is capable of taking this out. STANDANDELIVER (3) is close to a win after two successive placings, the latest a third over 1690m at this track. Great chance to break through. CINQUANTA (2) is worth some thought despite her last-start seventh over 1720m at Melton on July 24.",
